WEBVTT

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.377
Dad's missing I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:27.412 --> 00:00:28.605
I can't do this alone.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.046
Dad's giving us a job to do.

00:00:30.081 --> 00:00:32.071
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:32.106 --> 00:00:34.027
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:34.062 --> 00:00:37.020
This Demon killed mom and
Jess. I got to find dad.

00:00:37.055 --> 00:00:38.768
I've got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:38.803 --> 00:00:39.601
I'm Meg.

00:00:39.636 --> 00:00:40.628
So, where are you headed?

00:00:40.663 --> 00:00:41.620
No way I'm telling you.

00:00:41.621 --> 00:00:43.985
You could be some freak.

00:00:44.532 --> 00:00:45.805
Dad.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.764
<i>ust to get a glimpse
beyond this illusion</i>

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:50.981
<i>I was soaring ever</i>

00:00:51.016 --> 00:00:53.857
1835, Samuel Colt made a special gun.

00:00:53.892 --> 00:00:56.698
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:00:57.736 --> 00:01:01.422
<i>Though my eyes could see
I still was a blind man</i>

00:01:01.457 --> 00:01:05.108
<i>Though my mind could
think I still was a mad man</i>

00:01:05.143 --> 00:01:07.881
<i>I hear the voices when I'm dreaming</i>

00:01:07.916 --> 00:01:11.244
I have nightmares. And
sometime they come true.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:16.502
<i>Carry on my wayward son</i>

00:01:16.537 --> 00:01:18.497
<i>There'll be peace when you are</i>

00:01:18.532 --> 00:01:21.668
You two are all I've got. But I
guess we are stronger as a family.

00:01:21.703 --> 00:01:23.642
We go after this thing, together.

00:01:23.677 --> 00:01:24.145
Yes, sir.

00:01:24.146 --> 00:01:26.703
<i>Don't you cry no more</i>

00:01:51.641 --> 00:01:52.920
Good morning.

00:01:53.611 --> 00:01:55.274
Can I help you?

00:01:56.413 --> 00:01:58.390
I kind of...

00:01:58.425 --> 00:02:00.367
I need to talk.

00:02:02.115 --> 00:02:04.363
That's what I'm here for.

00:02:06.809 --> 00:02:09.431
I've done some things.

00:02:10.664 --> 00:02:12.330
Not good things.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:15.169
Well, there's always
forgiveness for us who seek it.

00:02:15.204 --> 00:02:17.351
For everyone?

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.661
Are you sure?

00:02:19.696 --> 00:02:21.409
I'll like to say...

00:02:21.444 --> 00:02:24.911
Salvation was created for sinners.

00:02:26.348 --> 00:02:29.402
Tell me what's on your mind.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:34.081
Well, I've lied a lot.

00:02:34.116 --> 00:02:36.156
I've Stolen.

00:02:36.191 --> 00:02:38.161
I've lusted...

00:02:38.196 --> 00:02:41.001
And the other day I met this man.

00:02:41.036 --> 00:02:44.744
A nice guy, you know?

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:51.448
We had a really good
chat. Sort of like this.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.237
And I slit his throat and ripped
his heart out through his chest.

00:02:58.272 --> 00:03:00.281
Does that make me a bad person?

00:03:00.316 --> 00:03:01.837
I know what you are.

00:03:03.965 --> 00:03:06.268
You can't be here.

00:03:06.303 --> 00:03:08.025
This is hollowed ground.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.534
Please...

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:12.721
Maybe that works in the minor leagues.

00:03:12.756 --> 00:03:15.399
But not with me.

00:03:40.057 --> 00:03:42.655
You throw like a girl.

00:03:43.478 --> 00:03:45.698
What do you want?

00:03:46.146 --> 00:03:48.825
The Winchesters.

00:03:48.992 --> 00:03:52.431
I haven't spoken to John
Winchester for over a year.

00:03:52.466 --> 00:03:54.475
You're wasting you time.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.528
Even if I knew where they were

00:03:56.563 --> 00:03:58.947
I'd never tell you.

00:03:58.982 --> 00:04:01.072
I know.

00:04:51.777 --> 00:04:53.334
So, this is it?

00:04:53.369 --> 00:04:55.637
This is everything I know.

00:04:55.672 --> 00:04:58.569
Look, our whole lives we've been
searching for this demon right?

00:04:58.604 --> 00:05:00.962
Not a trace. Just nothing.

00:05:00.997 --> 00:05:03.286
Until about a year ago.

00:05:03.321 --> 00:05:05.452
For the first time I picked up a trail.

00:05:05.487 --> 00:05:06.649
That's when you took off.

00:05:06.684 --> 00:05:07.586
Yeah.

00:05:07.621 --> 00:05:11.354
The demon must have come
out of hiding or hibernation.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.567
All right, so what's
this trail you've found?

00:05:13.602 --> 00:05:17.067
Starts in Arizona. Then
New Jersey, California.

00:05:17.102 --> 00:05:19.423
House is burned down to the ground.

00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:22.110
It's going after families.

00:05:22.145 --> 00:05:23.696
Just like it went after us.

00:05:23.731 --> 00:05:25.115
Families with infants?

00:05:25.116 --> 00:05:26.136
Yeah.

00:05:26.171 --> 00:05:29.220
The night of the kid's
six month birthday.

00:05:29.655 --> 00:05:31.325
I was six months old that night?

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.965
Exactly six months.

00:05:33.019 --> 00:05:38.416
So, basically this demon is going
after these kids for some reason.

00:05:39.148 --> 00:05:41.852
Same way it came for me.

00:05:42.597 --> 00:05:45.587
So, mom's death?

00:05:45.874 --> 00:05:47.440
Jessica, it's all because of me?

00:05:47.475 --> 00:05:48.342
We don't know that Sam.

00:05:48.343 --> 00:05:49.955
Oh, really? Cause I say
we're pretty damn sure Dean.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.413
For the last time. What happened
to them is not your fault.

00:05:52.448 --> 00:05:54.837
Yeah, you're right. It's not
my fault. But it's my problem.

00:05:54.872 --> 00:05:56.837
No, it's not your
problem. It's our problem.

00:05:56.872 --> 00:06:00.908
Okay. That's enough.

00:06:06.068 --> 00:06:07.862
So, why is it doing it?

00:06:07.897 --> 00:06:08.948
What does it want?

00:06:08.983 --> 00:06:11.701
I wish I had more answers. I do.

00:06:11.736 --> 00:06:14.385
I've always been one step behind it.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:18.060
Look I've never got
there in time to save...

00:06:23.248 --> 00:06:26.479
So how do we find it?
Before it hits again?

00:06:26.679 --> 00:06:28.647
There' re signs.

00:06:28.682 --> 00:06:30.214
Look, it took me a
while to see the patterns

00:06:30.249 --> 00:06:35.135
but days before these fires
signs crop up in an area.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:40.022
Cattle deaths, temperature
fluctuations, electrical storms.

00:06:40.577 --> 00:06:43.581
And then we backed and checked...

00:06:43.616 --> 00:06:46.887
These things happened in Lawrence?

00:06:46.922 --> 00:06:50.158
A week before your mother died.

00:06:52.041 --> 00:06:54.987
And in Palo Alto.

00:06:56.881 --> 00:06:59.308
Before Jessica.

00:06:59.343 --> 00:07:03.702
And these signs they're starting again.

00:07:04.086 --> 00:07:06.194
Where?

00:07:06.332 --> 00:07:09.325
Salvation, Iowa.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:42.385
Damn it!

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:43.416
What is it?

00:07:43.451 --> 00:07:44.571
Son of a bitch!

00:07:44.606 --> 00:07:45.692
What is it?

00:07:46.145 --> 00:07:47.676
I just got a call from Caleb.

00:07:47.711 --> 00:07:48.962
Is he okay?

00:07:48.997 --> 00:07:52.198
He's fine. Jim Murphy's dead.

00:07:52.233 --> 00:07:54.291
Pastor Jim?

00:07:55.342 --> 00:07:57.343
How?

00:07:57.378 --> 00:07:59.442
Throat was slashed.

00:07:59.477 --> 00:08:02.157
He bled out.

00:08:04.989 --> 00:08:08.009
Caleb said they found traces
of sulfur at Jim's place.

00:08:08.044 --> 00:08:09.620
The Demon?

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:11.971
The Demon?

00:08:12.006 --> 00:08:14.978
I don't know. Could be. He just got...

00:08:15.013 --> 00:08:18.075
He got careless he slipped up.

00:08:18.868 --> 00:08:22.287
Maybe the Demon knows
we're getting close.

00:08:22.322 --> 00:08:23.518
What do you want to do?

00:08:23.553 --> 00:08:25.886
Now we act like every second counts.

00:08:25.921 --> 00:08:28.995
There's two hospitals and a
health center in this County.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.053
We split up, we cover more ground.

00:08:31.088 --> 00:08:32.423
I want records.

00:08:32.458 --> 00:08:36.525
I want a list of every infant who's
gonna be six months old in the next week.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:38.521
Dad, that can be dozens of kids.

00:08:38.556 --> 00:08:40.410
How the hell are we gonna
know which one's the right one?

00:08:40.445 --> 00:08:43.051
We check them all. That's how.

00:08:43.543 --> 00:08:46.298
You got any better ideas?

00:08:47.822 --> 00:08:49.752
No, sir.

00:08:58.522 --> 00:08:59.939
Dad?

00:09:03.064 --> 00:09:05.123
Yeah.

00:09:06.667 --> 00:09:08.739
It's Jim.

00:09:09.113 --> 00:09:11.406
You know, I can't...

00:09:17.474 --> 00:09:19.638
This ends, now.

00:09:19.673 --> 00:09:21.767
I'm ending it.

00:09:21.802 --> 00:09:24.802
I don't care what it takes.

00:10:14.493 --> 00:10:15.704
Here you go, officer.

00:10:15.739 --> 00:10:16.853
Thank you.

00:10:32.957 --> 00:10:36.075
Hi, is there anything I can do for you?

00:10:36.434 --> 00:10:38.800
Oh, God, yes.

00:10:40.484 --> 00:10:43.092
Only I uh...

00:10:43.127 --> 00:10:46.044
Working right now, so...

00:11:36.237 --> 00:11:38.364
Train.

00:12:46.892 --> 00:12:48.175
Hi.

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:52.015
Here, let me hold that. I don't
think you need that anymore.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:54.666
She's gorgeous, is she yours?

00:12:54.701 --> 00:12:55.333
Yeah.

00:12:55.368 --> 00:12:56.863
Oh, wow. Hi.

00:12:56.864 --> 00:12:59.832
I'm sorry, I'm Sam. I
just moved in up the block.

00:12:59.867 --> 00:13:01.291
Oh, hey. I'm Monica.

00:13:01.326 --> 00:13:01.760
Monica.

00:13:01.761 --> 00:13:02.684
This is Rosy.

00:13:02.719 --> 00:13:03.277
Rosy?

00:13:03.278 --> 00:13:05.702
Yeah. So, welcome to the neighborhood.

00:13:05.737 --> 00:13:07.242
Thank you.

00:13:07.277 --> 00:13:08.800
She's such a good baby.

00:13:08.835 --> 00:13:10.989
I know, she... I mean, she never cries.

00:13:11.024 --> 00:13:13.197
She just stares at everybody.

00:13:13.232 --> 00:13:15.336
Sometimes she looks at you and...

00:13:15.371 --> 00:13:18.206
I swear it's like
she's reading your mind.

00:13:18.414 --> 00:13:20.873
What about you Monica?
Have you lived here long?

00:13:20.908 --> 00:13:23.914
Oh, my husband and I we bought this
place just before Rosy was born.

00:13:23.949 --> 00:13:25.159
How old is Rosy?

00:13:25.194 --> 00:13:27.108
She's six months today.

00:13:28.273 --> 00:13:31.412
It's big right? Growing like a weed.

00:13:31.447 --> 00:13:33.182
Yeah.

00:13:37.618 --> 00:13:39.624
Monica...

00:13:39.985 --> 00:13:41.750
Yeah?

00:13:43.713 --> 00:13:45.087
Just uh...

00:13:45.122 --> 00:13:46.892
Just take care of yourself, okay?

00:13:46.927 --> 00:13:49.225
Yeah, you too Sam. We'll see you around.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:49.744
Yeah.

00:13:51.479 --> 00:13:54.077
Oh, here's daddy!

00:14:58.728 --> 00:15:00.453
What are you...?

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:10.760
Rosy?

00:15:17.613 --> 00:15:19.525
No!

00:15:31.364 --> 00:15:33.333
A vision?

00:15:33.368 --> 00:15:35.289
Yes.

00:15:35.481 --> 00:15:38.640
I saw the Demon burning
a woman on the ceiling.

00:15:38.675 --> 00:15:41.107
Right and you think this is gonna
happen to this woman you met because...

00:15:41.142 --> 00:15:44.991
Because these things happen
exactly the way I see them.

00:15:45.026 --> 00:15:46.914
He started them as nightmares and...

00:15:46.949 --> 00:15:49.138
It started when he was awake.

00:15:49.173 --> 00:15:50.970
Yeah.

00:15:51.383 --> 00:15:54.592
It's like... I don't know,
it's like the closer I get...

00:15:54.627 --> 00:15:57.951
To anything involving the Demon
the stronger the visions get.

00:15:57.986 --> 00:16:01.045
All right, when were you
gonna tell me about this?

00:16:02.173 --> 00:16:03.592
We didn't know what it meant.

00:16:03.627 --> 00:16:08.665
All right, something like this starts happening to
your brother you pick up the phone and you call me.

00:16:09.111 --> 00:16:11.002
Call you?

00:16:11.791 --> 00:16:14.016
Are you kidding me?

00:16:14.808 --> 00:16:16.893
Dad, I called you from Lawrence.

00:16:16.928 --> 00:16:19.677
All right, Sam called
you when I was dying.

00:16:19.732 --> 00:16:23.193
I mean, getting you on the phone I got
a better chance winning the lottery.

00:16:28.548 --> 00:16:30.809
You're right.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:37.420
Although, I'm not crazy about this new
tone of yours, you're right. I'm sorry.

00:16:37.455 --> 00:16:38.875
Look, guys. Visions or no visions.

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:42.055
The fact is we know the
Demon is coming tonight.

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:45.195
And this family is going through
the same hell that we went through.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.864
No, they're not.

00:16:46.899 --> 00:16:50.260
No one is. Ever again.

00:16:56.663 --> 00:16:58.318
Hello.

00:16:58.353 --> 00:16:59.973
Sam?

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.603
Who is this?

00:17:01.638 --> 00:17:05.784
Think real hard, it'll come to you.

00:17:06.647 --> 00:17:08.478
Meg?

00:17:10.778 --> 00:17:13.061
Last time I saw you,
you fell out of a window.

00:17:13.096 --> 00:17:15.044
Yeah, thanks to you.

00:17:15.079 --> 00:17:17.400
That really hurt my feelings by the way.

00:17:17.435 --> 00:17:19.116
Just your feelings?

00:17:19.151 --> 00:17:21.719
That was a seven story drop.

00:17:21.754 --> 00:17:24.287
Let me speak to your dad.

00:17:26.763 --> 00:17:28.262
My dad?

00:17:28.297 --> 00:17:29.643
I don't know where my dad is.

00:17:29.678 --> 00:17:35.442
It's time for the grown ups to
talk, Sam. Let me speak to him, now.

00:17:44.112 --> 00:17:45.954
This is John.

00:17:45.989 --> 00:17:48.425
Howdy, John? I'm Meg.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.827
I'm a friend of your boys.

00:17:50.862 --> 00:17:54.518
I'm also the one who watched Jim
Murphy choke on his own blood.

00:17:57.185 --> 00:17:59.608
Still there, John boy?

00:17:59.643 --> 00:18:00.805
I'm here.

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:02.532
That was yesterday.

00:18:02.533 --> 00:18:05.118
Today I'm in Lincoln.

00:18:06.874 --> 00:18:10.160
Visiting another old friend of yours.

00:18:10.195 --> 00:18:13.175
He wants to say hi.

00:18:13.501 --> 00:18:15.315
John, whatever they do don't...

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:16.871
Caleb?

00:18:18.088 --> 00:18:20.049
Caleb?

00:18:20.479 --> 00:18:22.143
You listen to me...

00:18:22.178 --> 00:18:25.512
He's got nothing to do with
anything. You let him go.

00:18:25.547 --> 00:18:28.646
We know you have the Colt, John.

00:18:28.988 --> 00:18:31.016
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:18:31.051 --> 00:18:32.732
Oh?

00:18:32.767 --> 00:18:34.414
Okay.

00:18:35.016 --> 00:18:37.581
So, listen to this.

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:43.263
Caleb?

00:18:43.446 --> 00:18:44.509
Caleb?

00:18:44.544 --> 00:18:46.000
You hear that?

00:18:46.035 --> 00:18:47.842
That's the sound of your friend dying.

00:18:47.877 --> 00:18:49.961
Now, let's try this again.

00:18:49.996 --> 00:18:53.295
We know you have the gun,
John. Words travel fast.

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:57.367
So as far as we're concerned,
you just declared war.

00:18:57.402 --> 00:19:01.404
And this is what war looks
like. It has casualties.

00:19:02.243 --> 00:19:04.924
I'm gonna kill you, you know that?

00:19:04.959 --> 00:19:06.735
Oh, John. Please.

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:08.509
Mind your blood pressure.

00:19:08.544 --> 00:19:10.214
So, this is the thing.

00:19:10.249 --> 00:19:12.927
We're gonna keep doing what we're doing.

00:19:12.962 --> 00:19:14.680
And your friends...

00:19:14.715 --> 00:19:16.644
and anyone who has ever helped you?

00:19:16.679 --> 00:19:21.052
Gave you shelter, anyone you ever loved.

00:19:21.087 --> 00:19:25.426
They'll all die unless
you give us that gun.

00:19:29.119 --> 00:19:34.180
I'm waiting Johny. Better
answer before the buzzer.

00:19:34.633 --> 00:19:36.108
Okay.

00:19:36.143 --> 00:19:39.702
Sorry? I didn't quite get that.

00:19:39.737 --> 00:19:41.380
I said okay.

00:19:41.415 --> 00:19:43.915
I'll bring you the Colt.

00:19:44.246 --> 00:19:46.216
There's a warehouse in Lincoln.

00:19:46.251 --> 00:19:48.726
In the corner of Wellbasher and Lake.

00:19:48.761 --> 00:19:50.531
You're gonna meet me there.

00:19:50.566 --> 00:19:53.233
It's gonna take me about
a day's drive to get there.

00:19:53.268 --> 00:19:55.294
Meet me there at midnight tonight.

00:19:55.329 --> 00:19:56.033
That's impossible.

00:19:56.034 --> 00:19:58.995
I can't get there in time and I
can't just carry a gun on a plane.

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:03.007
Oh, then I guess your
friends die, don't they?

00:20:04.005 --> 00:20:06.114
If you do decide to make it...

00:20:06.149 --> 00:20:08.343
Come alone.

00:20:15.541 --> 00:20:18.889
What the hell are you looking at?

00:20:19.341 --> 00:20:21.534
So you think Meg is a demon?

00:20:21.569 --> 00:20:24.163
Either that or she's possessed by one.

00:20:24.198 --> 00:20:25.338
It doesn't really matter.

00:20:25.481 --> 00:20:25.481
What do we do?

00:20:25.516 --> 00:20:27.436
I'm going to Lincoln.

00:20:27.471 --> 00:20:28.353
What?

00:20:28.354 --> 00:20:30.231
Doesn't seem like I have a choice.

00:20:30.266 --> 00:20:33.856
If I don't go, a lot of
people die. Our friends die.

00:20:33.891 --> 00:20:36.133
Dad, the Demon is coming tonight.

00:20:36.168 --> 00:20:38.433
For Monica and her family
that gun is all we've got.

00:20:38.468 --> 00:20:40.238
You can't just hand it over.

00:20:40.273 --> 00:20:42.008
Who said about handing it over?

00:20:42.009 --> 00:20:44.878
Look, besides us and a couple of
vampires no one's really seen the gun.

00:20:44.913 --> 00:20:46.401
No one knows what it looks like.

00:20:46.436 --> 00:20:49.297
So what? You're just gonna
pick up a ringer in a pawn shop?

00:20:49.332 --> 00:20:51.779
Antique store.

00:20:51.987 --> 00:20:54.345
You're gonna hand Meg a fake
gun and hopes she doesn't notice?

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:56.435
Look, as long as it's close...

00:20:56.470 --> 00:20:58.169
She shouldn't be able
to tell the difference.

00:20:58.204 --> 00:21:00.922
Yeah, but for how long? What
happens when she figures it out?

00:21:00.957 --> 00:21:02.144
I just...

00:21:02.179 --> 00:21:05.333
I just need to buy a
few hours, that's all.

00:21:05.368 --> 00:21:08.512
You mean for Dean and me?

00:21:10.971 --> 00:21:14.783
You want us to stay here?

00:21:15.451 --> 00:21:17.732
And kill this Demon by ourselves.

00:21:17.767 --> 00:21:20.065
No, Sam.

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:22.843
I want to stop losing people we love.

00:21:22.878 --> 00:21:27.608
I want you to go to school I
want... I want Dean to have a home.

00:21:32.109 --> 00:21:35.790
I want Mary alive.

00:21:38.724 --> 00:21:40.831
It's just...

00:21:43.137 --> 00:21:47.046
I just want this to be over.

00:22:19.014 --> 00:22:20.847
Did you get it?

00:22:33.533 --> 00:22:36.168
You know this is a trap, don't you?

00:22:38.104 --> 00:22:39.843
That's why Meg wanted you to come alone.

00:22:39.878 --> 00:22:41.297
I can handle her.

00:22:41.332 --> 00:22:44.311
I have the wholed loaded.
Holy water, mandake, amu...

00:22:44.346 --> 00:22:45.807
Dad.

00:22:45.842 --> 00:22:47.269
What?

00:22:47.765 --> 00:22:49.384
Promise me something.

00:22:49.419 --> 00:22:51.509
What's that?

00:22:51.686 --> 00:22:55.726
If this doesn't go south
just get the hell out.

00:22:55.761 --> 00:23:00.034
Don't get yourself killed, all
right? You're no good to us dead.

00:23:02.741 --> 00:23:05.621
Same goes for you.

00:23:06.697 --> 00:23:09.066
All right, listen to me.

00:23:09.832 --> 00:23:13.409
They made the bullets
special for this Colt.

00:23:13.444 --> 00:23:15.697
Only four of them left.

00:23:15.732 --> 00:23:19.374
Without them, this gun is useless.

00:23:21.059 --> 00:23:23.149
You make every shot count.

00:23:23.184 --> 00:23:24.664
Yes, sir.

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:30.703
I've been waiting a
long time for this fight.

00:23:30.738 --> 00:23:34.956
Now it's here and I'm
not gonna be in it.

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:38.884
It's up to you boys now.

00:23:40.794 --> 00:23:43.339
It's your fight. You finish this.

00:23:43.374 --> 00:23:45.523
You finished what I started.

00:23:45.558 --> 00:23:47.919
You understand?

00:24:08.362 --> 00:24:11.059
We'll see you soon dad.

00:24:15.208 --> 00:24:16.905
I'll see you later.

00:24:41.883 --> 00:24:43.918
Later...

00:26:06.743 --> 00:26:08.894
Maybe we can tell them
there's a gas leak.

00:26:08.929 --> 00:26:11.577
Might get them out of
the house for a few hours.

00:26:11.612 --> 00:26:15.136
How many times did that work for us?

00:26:15.336 --> 00:26:16.887
Yeah.

00:26:20.117 --> 00:26:23.828
Could always tell them the truth.

00:26:25.531 --> 00:26:26.741
Na...

00:26:26.776 --> 00:26:27.952
I know.

00:26:27.953 --> 00:26:31.029
I know, I know, I just...

00:26:31.064 --> 00:26:32.968
What's to become of these people?

00:26:33.003 --> 00:26:35.434
Sam, we only got one move
and you know it, all right?

00:26:35.469 --> 00:26:37.866
We got to wait for that Demon
to show itself and then...

00:26:37.901 --> 00:26:40.912
We get it before it gets them.

00:26:44.870 --> 00:26:47.962
I wonder what dad's doing.

00:26:49.831 --> 00:26:53.803
I would feel a lot better if
we were there backing him up.

00:26:56.090 --> 00:27:00.200
I would feel a lot better
if he was here backing us up.

00:28:36.162 --> 00:28:38.418
This is what we have.

00:28:38.920 --> 00:28:40.740
What?

00:28:41.260 --> 00:28:44.777
After all those years
we're finally here.

00:28:44.812 --> 00:28:47.430
It doesn't seem real.

00:28:48.303 --> 00:28:52.129
We just got to keep our heads
and do our job like always.

00:28:52.164 --> 00:28:55.460
Yeah, but this isn't like always.

00:28:58.241 --> 00:29:00.331
True.

00:29:01.947 --> 00:29:04.272
Dean, uh...

00:29:06.976 --> 00:29:09.418
I want to thank you.

00:29:10.473 --> 00:29:13.047
For what?

00:29:15.105 --> 00:29:17.643
For everything.

00:29:17.678 --> 00:29:19.852
You've always led my back you know.

00:29:19.887 --> 00:29:24.199
Even when I can't count on anyone
I could always count on you.

00:29:24.234 --> 00:29:26.288
And now...

00:29:26.643 --> 00:29:29.341
I don't know, I just
want to let you know.

00:29:29.376 --> 00:29:30.650
Just incase.

00:29:30.685 --> 00:29:33.115
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Are you kidding me?

00:29:33.150 --> 00:29:34.167
What?

00:29:34.202 --> 00:29:36.315
Don't say just incase
something happens to you.

00:29:36.350 --> 00:29:38.429
I don't want to hear
that freaking speech man.

00:29:38.464 --> 00:29:40.615
Nobody is dying tonight.

00:29:40.650 --> 00:29:43.723
Not us, not that family, nobody.

00:29:44.324 --> 00:29:46.575
Except that Demon.

00:29:46.610 --> 00:29:51.502
That evil son of a bitch ain't getting
any older than tonight. You understand me?

00:30:02.757 --> 00:30:04.949
John. You made it.

00:30:04.984 --> 00:30:07.106
Too bad really.

00:30:07.141 --> 00:30:09.569
I was hoping to kill
more of your friends.

00:30:09.604 --> 00:30:11.796
Sorry to disappoint.

00:30:11.831 --> 00:30:15.502
I can see where your
boys get their good looks.

00:30:15.537 --> 00:30:21.570
I must admit, considering what they
say about you I thought you'd be taller.

00:30:24.051 --> 00:30:26.823
Well, aren't you the chatty one?

00:30:26.858 --> 00:30:29.595
You want to get to business?

00:30:30.236 --> 00:30:31.939
Fine.

00:30:32.652 --> 00:30:34.591
Why don't you hand over the gun?

00:30:34.626 --> 00:30:37.593
If I give you the gun,
how do I get out of here?

00:30:37.628 --> 00:30:41.674
If you're as good as they say you are,
I'm sure you'll figure something out.

00:30:41.709 --> 00:30:43.618
Maybe I'll just shoot you.

00:30:43.653 --> 00:30:46.250
You want to shoot me, baby? Go ahead.

00:30:46.285 --> 00:30:51.327
It won't end anything.
There's more where I came from.

00:30:55.495 --> 00:30:57.061
Who the hell's that?

00:30:57.096 --> 00:31:01.435
He's not as nearly as much fun
as I am, I can tell you that.

00:31:01.470 --> 00:31:05.286
So, I suggest you give us the gun.

00:31:11.449 --> 00:31:13.786
Now!

00:31:24.044 --> 00:31:26.232
This is the Colt?

00:31:31.736 --> 00:31:34.272
What do you think?

00:31:55.569 --> 00:31:57.922
You shot me!

00:31:58.506 --> 00:32:02.089
I can't believe you just shot me!

00:32:03.321 --> 00:32:05.609
It's a fake!

00:32:15.475 --> 00:32:16.982
You're dead John.

00:32:17.017 --> 00:32:18.455
You're boys are dead.

00:32:18.490 --> 00:32:21.466
I never used the gun. How can
I know it would never work?

00:32:21.501 --> 00:32:24.443
I'm so not in the mood for
this. I've just been shot!

00:32:24.478 --> 00:32:27.371
Well I guess you're
lucky the gun wasn't real.

00:32:27.406 --> 00:32:29.164
That's funny, John.

00:32:29.199 --> 00:32:34.603
We're gonna strip the skin from
your bones but that was funny.

00:33:19.008 --> 00:33:21.561
Holy water, John.

00:33:21.596 --> 00:33:24.457
Real cute.

00:33:34.660 --> 00:33:37.241
Dad's not answering.

00:33:40.216 --> 00:33:42.133
Maybe Meg was late.

00:33:42.168 --> 00:33:43.756
Maybe the reception is bad.

00:33:43.791 --> 00:33:45.098
Yeah, well...

00:33:50.513 --> 00:33:52.715
Dean, wait.

00:33:53.599 --> 00:33:55.281
Listen.

00:34:18.309 --> 00:34:20.451
It's coming.

00:34:28.279 --> 00:34:29.832
Damn it.

00:34:57.769 --> 00:34:59.502
Get out of my house!

00:35:00.788 --> 00:35:02.522
Get out of my house!

00:35:04.482 --> 00:35:05.561
Mr. Hold, please.

00:35:05.596 --> 00:35:06.493
Be quite and listen to me.

00:35:06.494 --> 00:35:08.710
Be quite and listen to me.
We are trying to help you.

00:35:08.745 --> 00:35:09.714
Charlie?

00:35:09.749 --> 00:35:10.683
Okay?

00:35:10.684 --> 00:35:11.821
Everything okay down there?

00:35:11.856 --> 00:35:12.830
Monica, get the baby!

00:35:12.831 --> 00:35:14.007
Don't go over there!

00:35:14.042 --> 00:35:15.183
You stay away from her!

00:35:21.213 --> 00:35:23.559
What are you..

00:35:38.325 --> 00:35:39.758
Where the hell did it go?

00:35:39.793 --> 00:35:40.293
My baby!

00:35:40.328 --> 00:35:41.800
No, hey wait.

00:35:41.801 --> 00:35:43.740
Get her out of here, I got it.

00:35:44.010 --> 00:35:45.219
Come on.

00:35:45.254 --> 00:35:46.213
My baby!

00:35:46.248 --> 00:35:47.279
Dean's got her.

00:36:43.638 --> 00:36:45.623
You get away from my family!

00:36:45.658 --> 00:36:47.608
Charlie, don't. They saved us.

00:36:47.643 --> 00:36:49.255
They saved us...

00:36:57.130 --> 00:36:58.981
Thank you.

00:37:03.067 --> 00:37:04.733
It's still in there.

00:37:05.013 --> 00:37:06.128
Sam, Sam. No!

00:37:06.163 --> 00:37:07.504
Dean, let me go. It's still in there!

00:37:07.539 --> 00:37:08.845
It's burning to the
ground. It's suicide!

00:37:08.880 --> 00:37:09.714
I don't care!

00:37:09.749 --> 00:37:11.043
I do!

00:37:27.027 --> 00:37:30.889
Come on, dad. Answer
your phone, damn it!

00:37:34.494 --> 00:37:36.989
Something's wrong.

00:37:39.094 --> 00:37:41.266
You hear me? Something's happened.

00:37:41.301 --> 00:37:43.438
If you had just let me go in there...

00:37:43.473 --> 00:37:46.678
I could have ended all this.

00:37:46.713 --> 00:37:48.092
Sam...

00:37:48.127 --> 00:37:51.227
The only thing you
would end was your life.

00:37:51.905 --> 00:37:54.262
You don't know that.

00:37:54.297 --> 00:37:57.914
So what? You're willing to
sacrifice yourself? Is that it?

00:37:58.423 --> 00:38:00.665
Yeah. Yeah, you're damn right I am.

00:38:00.700 --> 00:38:02.907
Yeah, well that's not gonna
happen. Not as long as I'm around.

00:38:02.942 --> 00:38:04.451
What the hell are you
talking about Dean?

00:38:04.486 --> 00:38:07.217
We've been searching for
this Demon our whole lives.

00:38:07.252 --> 00:38:08.858
It's the only thing
we've ever cared about.

00:38:08.893 --> 00:38:11.667
Sam, I want to waste it. I do, okay?

00:38:11.702 --> 00:38:13.661
But it's not worth dying over?

00:38:13.696 --> 00:38:14.215
What?

00:38:14.250 --> 00:38:15.565
I mean it.

00:38:15.566 --> 00:38:19.035
If hunting this Demon means
you getting yourself killed.

00:38:19.070 --> 00:38:21.417
Then I hope we never
find the damn thing.

00:38:21.452 --> 00:38:24.433
That thing killed Jess.

00:38:25.335 --> 00:38:28.095
That thing killed mom.

00:38:28.563 --> 00:38:31.478
You said yourself once.

00:38:31.629 --> 00:38:34.621
That no matter what we do they're gone

00:38:34.656 --> 00:38:37.063
and they're never coming back.

00:38:37.521 --> 00:38:40.284
Don't just say that! Don't you!

00:38:40.319 --> 00:38:43.047
After all this, don't you say that.

00:38:44.629 --> 00:38:48.230
Sam, look.

00:38:48.265 --> 00:38:51.082
The three of us...

00:38:51.285 --> 00:38:54.081
That's all we have.

00:38:55.587 --> 00:38:58.611
It's all I have.

00:39:01.834 --> 00:39:06.092
Sometimes I feel like I'm
barely holding it together, man.

00:39:06.954 --> 00:39:09.846
Without you and dad...

00:39:10.820 --> 00:39:12.889
Dad...

00:39:17.975 --> 00:39:20.351
He should have called by now.

00:39:20.386 --> 00:39:22.851
Try again.

00:39:39.377 --> 00:39:43.189
You boys really screwed up this time.

00:39:46.058 --> 00:39:48.408
Where is he?

00:39:48.588 --> 00:39:51.840
You're never gonna
see your father again.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
